ent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues.\n\nStrengths: reliability (conscientious), stress resilience, technical (weather, computers). Concerns: memory for numbers (attention), nasty remarks (crew cooperation, professional communication).\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership, regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas.\n\nStrengths: anticipation (decision quality, safety), complex connections (technical competence), leadership. Concerns: show-off (crew cooperation), not open to new ideas (adaptability).\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as know-it-all, hot temper.\n\nStrengths: problem solving, responsibility, concentration. Concerns: hot temper, know-it-all (crew cooperation).\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate B has strong reliability and stress handling but has nasty remarks, which is serious for crew cooperation. Candidate A has good decision and calm but poor communication and egocentric. Candidate C has strong anticipation and leadership but not open to new ideas and show-off. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but hot temper and know-it-all.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate B's conscientiousness and stress handling outweigh communication issues? But nasty remarks could be severe. Candidate A's egocentric and unwillingness to learn are concerning for long-term development. Candidate C's lack of openness is concerning for adaptability. Candidate D's hot temper is concerning for stress resilience.\n\nThus maybe Candidate B is still strongest overall, with some concerns that could be mitigated. So vote for Candidate B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: there is none, but we can say \"To start, I think...\" That's okay.\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
